WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:03.400
(rain pattering)

00:00:15.424 --> 00:00:19.341
(diners chatting and laughing)

00:00:27.926 --> 00:00:31.009
(heartbeat thumping)

00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:04.540
- It's hard to take action.

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:06.050
It's painful.

00:01:06.050 --> 00:01:08.810
(pensive music)
Washing the dishes isn't fun.

00:01:08.810 --> 00:01:11.450
Meditation can be tedious.

00:01:11.450 --> 00:01:13.940
Waking up early is hard.
(alarm ringing)

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:16.770
The discomfort we feel
in the face of action

00:01:16.770 --> 00:01:19.950
often paralyzes us from
doing anything at all,

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:21.490
so we sleep in.

00:01:21.490 --> 00:01:23.250
We get lost in the rabbit hole

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:26.040
of YouTube, TikTok, Instagram,

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:29.650
letting clickbait decide for
us what our next move will be

00:01:29.650 --> 00:01:32.440
while our lives slip into disarray.

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:34.650
We resign to inaction

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:37.710
as the solution to avoid
the pain of action,

00:01:37.710 --> 00:01:39.520
subconsciously aware of the fact

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:42.400
that our stagnation breeds destruction.

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:44.270
By avoiding the pain of action,

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:47.020
we allow something worse to fester:

00:01:47.020 --> 00:01:50.500
the horror of watching
opportunities pass us by.

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:52.690
Our relationships grow distant,

00:01:52.690 --> 00:01:55.853
our bills stack up, our families grow old.

00:01:57.280 --> 00:01:58.920
Pain is all around us.

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:01.680
It's as much a part of
life as death itself.

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:05.110
No matter how impoverished
or affluent your upbringing,

00:02:05.110 --> 00:02:06.750
pain is inescapable.

00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:08.760
It'll follow you wherever you go.

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:10.350
And this sobering reality

00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:13.030
leads many into nihilism and despair.

00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:14.390
But not everyone knows

00:02:14.390 --> 00:02:16.620
that there's another
way to look at things.

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:18.380
Pain can be bargained with.

00:02:18.380 --> 00:02:21.230
It takes from us, but
it can also give back.

00:02:21.230 --> 00:02:24.363
It just depends on which
pain we choose to embrace.

00:02:25.718 --> 00:02:27.390
(bright music)
There are two types of pain:

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:30.340
the pain of action and
the pain of inaction.

00:02:30.340 --> 00:02:33.490
The pain of action is blunt, in your face,

00:02:33.490 --> 00:02:35.420
and forces you to grow.

00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:38.690
For every hour we suffer
through sharpening our skills,

00:02:38.690 --> 00:02:41.280
being proactive, and restoring order,

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:44.090
we don't reduce the
amount of pain we face,

00:02:44.090 --> 00:02:46.090
but rather we take it on the chin,

00:02:46.090 --> 00:02:48.240
we sign up for it up front.

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:50.940
And because of this voluntary acceptance,

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:54.500
day after day we gain the
strength to shoulder it.

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:57.470
By embracing pain instead
of running from it,

00:02:57.470 --> 00:03:00.450
we are simultaneously transformed by it.

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:02.840
We become someone we are proud of,

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:05.110
someone that others can depend upon,

00:03:05.110 --> 00:03:07.710
which in turn gives meaning to the pain.

00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:10.310
And it's this feeling
of growth and progress

00:03:10.310 --> 00:03:14.490
that helps us feel useful to
ourselves, useful to others,

00:03:14.490 --> 00:03:16.673
which gives the suffering a purpose.

00:03:17.657 --> 00:03:20.407
(wind whistling)

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:26.150
The pain of inaction, however,

00:03:26.150 --> 00:03:30.226
is the pain that eats
away at you, a poison.

00:03:30.226 --> 00:03:31.890
(forlorn music)
It's slow-burning,

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:35.170
draining your will and decaying your soul.

00:03:35.170 --> 00:03:40.050
By descending into apathy,
things disintegrate. Entropy.

00:03:40.050 --> 00:03:44.840
By letting ourselves go, we
lose self-respect. Negligence.

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:48.200
By vegging out on the
couch for days on end,

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:50.340
things fall into disorder.

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:52.930
Inaction is the holiday of fools

00:03:52.930 --> 00:03:55.000
who trade temporary discomfort

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:57.663
for long-term existential suffering.

00:03:58.530 --> 00:04:00.530
So which pain will we choose?

00:04:00.530 --> 00:04:03.050
Action is a life-giving breath;

00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:04.723
inaction is a slow death.

